  "body": "The earlier positive J0 candidate sample did not determine the response sign: it subtracts terms near 1.75e21, and a boundary interpolation defect is larger than the sample. This checkpoint preserves the exact registered displacement correlation, evaluates the complete second constant-operator feedback, and bounds the remaining actual-coefficient response error. The resulting conditional J0 and N0 shell intervals are negative at x=9/8 and x=5/4.\n\nAt x=9/8, the complete proper-time clock and quadratic first-order terms also give a negative anchored-volume second parameter derivative. This is a smooth kinematical jet under the retained projection assumptions; it supplies neither a finite-amplitude volume change nor the missing angular Einstein solution or cosmological evidence.\n\nValidation: all seven upstream closures authenticated before/after computation; exact positive 5/10-state resolvents; complete input/source/coefficient and third-and-higher feedback accounting; fixed 256-subinterval outward quadrature; independent moment, noncommuting-matrix and volume-interval reviews. The packaged source archive replays the bounded calculations normally and under `-O`, compares reference bytes, and rejects altered-source controls. The dedicated workflow repeats that replay.\n\nAdds a self-contained source capsule, derivations, internal review evidence and replay workflow. README and English/Spanish status additions have exact removal-to-base checks. Frozen research capsules, papers, workflows and unrelated projects are preserved. No new Zenodo version or journal submission accompanies this checkpoint.\n",
